web888-redpitaya (2025.430-3) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Shared safe FPGA selector/loader (web888-ng Phase 2 lane B):
    - New /usr/lib/web888/web888-fpga-select (root-owned), the single owner
      of the runtime FPGA selection: `status` (persisted profile reported
      separately from the active service, never inferred from prog_done),
      `select stock` (persist default, remove the staged open snapshot,
      never writes the PL), `select web888-ng-hf --experimental`
      (double consent gate: root-owned /etc/web888/fpga-experimental must
      authorize the exact profile+SHA-256 of the open HF bitstream AND the
      command needs --experimental; the verified artifact is snapshotted
      immutably — root-owned regular file 0444, never a symlink — into
      /var/lib/web888-fpga/, so a later package update cannot silently
      change the consented contents), `load` (lock-serialized, refuses
      while a conflicting SDR service is active, programs /dev/xdevcfg from
      the persisted selection with a prog_done timeout, fail closed —
      intended as the root ExecStartPre of web888-web888d.service, which
      then runs --bitstream none).
    - web888-mode: three-way websdr/web888d/<rp-app> switching with
      optional --fpga stock|web888-ng-hf [--experimental]; no --fpga keeps
      the persisted selection (initial default stock); an FPGA change stops
      ALL stacks before select/load/start even when APP is unchanged; a
      same mode+FPGA switch is a no-op; --fpga is rejected for RP apps.
      stop/status/list handle web888d.
    - web888-rpapp@.service + websdr drop-in 50-redpitaya.conf: add
      Conflicts=web888-web888d.service.
    - postinst: create /var/lib/web888-fpga (root:root 0755) and default the
      selection to stock on fresh installs only; upgrades never change the
      selection or touch services.

 -- SteamedFish <steamedfish@hotmail.com>  Sat, 01 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0800

web888-redpitaya (2025.430-2) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Hardware-gate fix: patch 0001-peri-use-zynqsdr-ioctl —
    sdr_receiver_hpsdr's peri.c drove the PE4312 DSA via sysfs GPIO
    523/525/524, but the zynqsdr kernel driver owns MIO 11/12/13 on this
    image (EBUSY → vendor code dereferenced a NULL FILE* and SEGV'd).
    peri.c now uses the driver's ZYNQSDR_AD8370_SET ioctl (step-2
    hw-gate proven, PL-bitstream-agnostic) and returns -1 on failure
    instead of crashing.
  * web888-rpapp@.service: + StartLimitIntervalSec=120 StartLimitBurst=10 —
    a hardware-gate SEGV crash-loop reloaded the bitstream every ~4s for ~15min
    (sustained devcfg churn, device later found hung); cap restarts so a
    failing app gives up instead of churning the PL.

 -- SteamedFish <steamedfish@hotmail.com>  Thu, 06 Aug 2026 01:30:00 +0800

web888-redpitaya (2025.430-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian package of the Web-888 Red Pitaya app stack
    (step 4, Red Pitaya coexistence):
    - C servers built from source: RaspSDR/red-pitaya-notes @ da1a7e3a
      (2025-04-30, MIT): sdr-receiver, sdr-receiver-hpsdr,
      sdr-transceiver-wide; si5351-init from scripts/hw-test/si5351.
    - Vendored factory bitstreams (Vivado 2023.1, 2024/12): led_blinker,
      sdr_receiver, sdr_receiver_hpsdr, sdr_transceiver_wide
      (/usr/share/web888-redpitaya/apps/<app>/<app>.bit).
    - web888-rpapp@.service template: root (required for /dev/mem),
      bitstream load in ExecStartPre via load-bitstream (prog_done
      poll, fail closed), Conflicts=web888-websdr.service; drop-in
      50-redpitaya.conf declares the reverse conflict on the websdr
      unit. No [Install] — never auto-enabled.
    - /usr/sbin/web888-mode runtime switch (websdr/<app>/stop/list).
    - /etc/web888-redpitaya/switch.conf conffile: SI5351_RESET=0
      default until hardware measurement settles the requirement.

